1
00:00:04,978 --> 00:00:07,356
I'm so glad everyone is asleep.

2
00:00:07,356 --> 00:00:11,912
I thought Max would be crying, and everybody would be awake.

3
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,712
What did I tell you?

4
00:00:13,712 --> 00:00:15,837
Nothing to worry about.

5
00:00:15,837 --> 00:00:19,154
I'm sure everything is fine.

6
00:00:19,154 --> 00:00:38,714
My mother knows all there is to know

7
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:43,192
about taking care of babies, I assure you.

8
00:00:43,192 --> 00:00:46,029
Let's put some of this stuff away and then take off.

9
00:00:46,029 --> 00:00:48,454
We've got a forty-minute drive into the city.

10
00:00:48,454 --> 00:00:48,992
Welcome home--

11
00:00:48,992 --> 00:00:50,625
and I do mean welcome home.

12
00:00:50,625 --> 00:00:51,069
Something wrong?

13
00:00:51,069 --> 00:00:51,958
Oh, nothing's wrong, Richard.

14
00:00:51,958 --> 00:00:53,963
Believe me, Max is fine.

15
00:00:53,963 --> 00:01:02,537
But his teeth hurt, and he just can't get to sleep, poor dear.

16
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:06,235
Neither can you.

17
00:01:06,235 --> 00:01:08,035
Oh, I feel so bad.

18
00:01:08,035 --> 00:01:14,449
Oh, I'm fine.

19
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:17,427
How was your weekend?

20
00:01:17,427 --> 00:01:20,734
We had a great time, Mom.

21
00:01:20,734 --> 00:01:20,934
It was wonderful.

22
00:01:20,734 --> 00:01:22,405
The weather couldn't have been better.

23
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:27,028
It was nice here, too.

24
00:01:27,028 --> 00:01:34,317
Did you get a chance to get outside at all?

25
00:01:34,317 --> 00:01:35,117
Oh, yes.

26
00:01:35,117 --> 00:01:36,628
Grandpa helped me yesterday afternoon.

27
00:01:36,628 --> 00:01:40,273
I went to the supermarket to get a few things,

28
00:01:40,273 --> 00:01:42,938
and I stayed out an extra half hour.

29
00:01:42,938 --> 00:01:45,729
The village was filled with people--the weather was so nice.

30
00:01:45,729 --> 00:01:47,636
Harry's a professional camper, Mom. Harry

31
00:01:47,636 --> 00:01:49,136
He knows all there is to know,

32
00:01:49,136 --> 00:01:52,105
and he made the weekend very easy for us to enjoy.

33
00:01:52,105 --> 00:01:54,663
Come on. You all helped.

34
00:01:54,663 --> 00:01:57,140
You were wonderful, Harry!

35
00:01:57,140 --> 00:02:00,185
Why don't you go to your room, Mom, and get some sleep.

36
00:02:00,185 --> 00:02:00,825
Oh, I'm fine.

37
00:02:00,825 --> 00:02:03,029
Tell me more about your weekend.

38
00:02:03,029 --> 00:02:08,052
Did you do anything special?

39
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:09,269
Lots of special country things.

40
00:02:09,269 --> 00:02:09,999
We picked flowers.

41
00:02:09,999 --> 00:02:14,008
And we brought some home for you.

42
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:16,986
It was so nice to be out in the country.

43
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:19,466
They smell wonderful.

44
00:02:19,466 --> 00:02:20,631
Everything smelled so special.

45
00:02:20,631 --> 00:02:33,174
It would have been great if we had been able to bottle the smells.

46
00:02:33,174 --> 00:02:39,582
It would be a great business if you could do that.

47
00:02:39,582 --> 00:02:40,810
Oh!

48
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:44,988
Uh, we're home now, Ellen.

49
00:02:44,988 --> 00:02:46,766
We'll take care of it.

50
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:49,744
I'll take care of it.

51
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,264
Let's see if it works.

52
00:02:51,264 --> 00:02:52,722
What's that?

53
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:56,000
A little special country music.

54
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,400
I think we'd better head home.

55
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,958
It's getting late, and we have a bit of a drive.

56
00:03:00,958 --> 00:03:03,656
Well, all your things are inside.

57
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:04,634
There's your sleeping bag.

58
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:08,112
Oh, thanks, Harry.

59
00:03:08,112 --> 00:03:10,012
Say good-bye to Richard.

60
00:03:10,012 --> 00:03:12,089
We'll call you all tomorrow night.

61
00:03:12,089 --> 00:03:13,089
Good-bye.

62
00:03:13,089 --> 00:03:19,523
Bye, Mom.

63
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:25,479
I'm so tired I think I'm overtired.

64
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:37,391
I don't know if I can get to sleep.

65
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,369
Max has stopped crying. Max

66
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:43,347
Yes. It works!

67
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:46,325
It works!

68
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:48,325
What works?

69
00:03:48,325 --> 00:03:55,259
This.

70
00:03:55,259 --> 00:04:04,193
Oh. Oh, where did you get that?

71
00:04:04,193 --> 00:04:13,127
It sounds so nice.

72
00:04:13,127 --> 00:04:28,016
I think I'm falling asleep.

73
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:29,516
Like Max did.

74
00:04:29,516 --> 00:04:31,482
Good night.

75
00:04:31,482 --> 00:05:40,887
Sounds of the country.

76
00:05:40,887 --> 00:05:43,887
The soothing sounds of the country.
